<title>SWEDEN: Incentive says Gambro buys 9 U.S. clinics.</title>
<headline>Incentive says Gambro buys 9 U.S. clinics.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish investment company Incentive AB said on Tuesday its Gambro health care equipment unit had bought nine dialysis clinics from Massachusetts-based  International Health Specialists (IHS).  </p>
<p>No financial details were given.</p>
<p>&quot;The clinics are contracted to provide dialysis for four rehabilitation hospitals as well as to perform 6,000 acute dialysis treatments annually,&quot; Incentive said in a statement.</p>
<p>After the acquisition, Gambro Healthcare owns 97 clinics with around 8,400 patients, it said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
